    {
      "post_id": 48648,
      "author_username": "meizzwang",
      "author_user_id": 11,
      "timestamp_iso": "2022-07-26T23:09:35+00:00",
      "timestamp_epoch_ms": 1658876975000,
      "timestamp_raw": "Jul 26, 2022 18:09:35 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "The absolute biggest PITA to grow, I've been losing divisions to rot consistently every year for as long as I can remember!  This is definitely one of the top 10 most difficult clones in the collection to keep alive, even when it's watered perfectly and left completely alone.    I think the second this clone is divided, it becomes  super susceptible to rot, even if the mother plant it came from was rot free for years!    There is one other backup division that I have kept in anther tray that hasn't been disturbed or divided for several years and it has had zero rot issues, so maybe I just have to stop dividing these plants?    It's a tough thing to do since so many people want one, and I'm not the hoarder type despite all pictures suggesting otherwise  <img alt=\":)\" class=\"smile\" src=\"//storage.proboards.com/forum/images/smiley/smiley.png\"/><br/><br/>S. alata Lemon yellow Jasper Co, TX looking really yellow this time around!  Pics taken 7/19/22:<br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52244228505_97c99e7c27_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52243737541_ceca01b6b7_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52244228235_cbdbc0f64f_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/>",
      "body_text": "The absolute biggest PITA to grow, I've been losing divisions to rot consistently every year for as long as I can remember!  This is definitely one of the top 10 most difficult clones in the collection to keep alive, even when it's watered perfectly and left completely alone.    I think the second this clone is divided, it becomes  super susceptible to rot, even if the mother plant it came from was rot free for years!    There is one other backup division that I have kept in anther tray that hasn't been disturbed or divided for several years and it has had zero rot issues, so maybe I just have to stop dividing these plants?    It's a tough thing to do since so many people want one, and I'm not the hoarder type despite all pictures suggesting otherwise\nS. alata Lemon yellow Jasper Co, TX looking really yellow this time around!  Pics taken 7/19/22:",
